From: pVisor contributors
Subject: [PATCH] sched/deadline: backport fair-server idle stop and correctness fixes

Backport Linux upstream e636ffb9e31b (time accounting), f5a538c07df2
(idle stop), and ca1e8eede4fc (runnable-task stop race) to 6.12.109.
Original authors: Peter Zijlstra <peterz@infradead.org> and
Gabriele Monaco <gmonaco@redhat.com>. GPL-2.0-only.

Adapt rq->donor to rq->curr (no proxy scheduling in this tree), idle_rq
to idle_cpu(cpu_of(rq)) (checks current, nr_running and ttwu_pending),
and retain 6.12's lazy server initialization. Clear dl_defer_idle before
the active-server early return. No timer filtering, Agent API, PSI or
network watchdog policy changes.

Upstream:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/e636ffb9e31b4f7dde7fef5358669266b9ce02ec
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/f5a538c07df26f5c601e41f7b9c7ade3e1e75803
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/ca1e8eede4fc68ce85a9fdce1a6c13ad64933318

